/* indicator.rcss - IndicatorPanel layout, from the old
   abcenchance/res/IndicatorPanel.res (400x400 panel centered with c-200
   anchors; four 200x100 images at xpos 100 ypos 150, per-slot offset 30/40/
   50/50). The img rides 150-off dp above the pivot in unrotated space (old
   IndicatorImage::Paint: y in [50-off, 150-off], screen y = pivot_y - y).

   The transform pivot is the screen center: the old math rotated the image
   quad about the container's top-left corner, which sits exactly at the
   screen center (container origin = center - (100, 50) with the rotation
   folded back by the containerW/2, containerH/2 shift).

   Texture orientation (P5 audit): the old DrawTexturePos mapped the stored
   97x260 crescent through texcoords whose u/v axes are swapped against the
   vertex order (p1=screen top-left gets (0,0) but p2=screen top-right gets
   (0,1)) - the composite is the stored image TRANSPOSED across its main
   diagonal: a shallow arch over the pivot bulging up at angle 0. The shipped
   pain_indicator.png is pre-transposed (260x97) so the plain upright img
   reproduces that composite byte for byte (D-17 note).

   RmlUi 6.3 has no calc(): each rotor is a 2000dp box whose center is
   placed on the panel center with a -50% margin pair (the box is invisible
   itself and big enough to cover the viewport under any rotation angle). */

#indicator {
	position: absolute;
	left: 50%;
	top: 50%;
	margin-left: -200dp;
	margin-top: -200dp;
	width: 400dp;
	height: 400dp;
}

#indicator .rotor {
	position: absolute;
	left: 50%;
	top: 50%;
	margin-left: -1000dp;
	margin-top: -1000dp;
	width: 2000dp;
	height: 2000dp;
	transform-origin: 50% 50%;
	display: none;
}

#indicator .pain {
	display: block;
	position: absolute;
	width: 200dp;
	height: 100dp;
	left: 50%;
	margin-left: -100dp;
	top: 50%;
	/* top margin = -(150 - offset)dp; offsets 30/40/50/50 (old res). */
	/* Old scheme Indicator.FgColor = 255 0 0 255. */
	image-color: #ff0000;
}
#rotor-1 .pain { margin-top: -120dp; }
#rotor-2 .pain { margin-top: -110dp; }
#rotor-3 .pain { margin-top: -100dp; }
#rotor-4 .pain { margin-top: -100dp; }
